{"description":"Read a Google Doc as markdown + inline HTML. The read opens with a <style> block \u2014 one CSS rule per named style (p = Normal text, h1\u2013h6, .title, .subtitle), in pt \u2014 and a paragraph or run shows style=\"\u2026\" only where it differs from its rule (text-align, line-height, margin-top/bottom/left/right, text-indent; a hanging indent is margin-left:36pt with a negative text-indent). Title and Subtitle paragraphs read as <p class=\"title\">. A page break reads as <div style=\"page-break-after:always\"></div> on its own line, where the break is. Every element in a paragraph reads, so an edit that quotes one can give it back: a footnote is [^1] with its note as a [^1]: line at the end; a date is <time datetime=\"2026-11-15\">Nov 15, 2026</time>; a person or a link chip is <a class=\"chip\" href=\"mailto:jane@x.com\">Jane Doe</a> (the text is Google\u2019s); a dropdown is <input class=\"chip\" list=\"kix.\u2026\" value=\"Draft\"> with its list as a <datalist id=\"kix.\u2026\" title=\"Status\"><option>Draft</option></datalist> line after the <style> block; a horizontal rule is --- on a line of its own; a column break is <span style=\"break-after:column\"></span>; an equation and a page-number field are empty <span class=\"equation\"> and <span class=\"page-number\"> whose title says to edit them in Google Docs. A table of contents is not read. List items show no indent: their nesting owns it. mode: clean (committed text, default) \u00b7 tracked (suggestions shown as <ins>/<del>) \u00b7 accepted \u00b7 rejected. segment picks the content tree: body (default), header, footer, or all (body plus every header/footer, each labelled). Text that would otherwise read as markup is marked as literal: a paragraph wrapped in <p>\u2026</p> (\"4. Term\" is a paragraph, not a list) or a backslash before a character (5 \\* 3), and \\\\ is a real backslash \u2014 write them back as read, and the document keeps only the words. A body read always reports which headers/footers exist and what they hold, since their content \u2014 a letterhead logo, a page number \u2014 is NOT part of the body and would otherwise be invisible.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"account":{"description":"Google account email to use. Defaults to GDOCS_DEFAULT_ACCOUNT, or the sole account.","type":"string"},"mode":{"description":"read mode (default clean)","enum":["clean","tracked","accepted","rejected"],"type":"string"},"page":{"description":"which header/footer, when a doc defines more than one (default-page, first-page, even-page). Omit to use whichever exists.","enum":["default","first","even"],"type":"string"},"path":{"description":"The doc or tab: a Drive id or URL, /folder/doc, or /folder/doc/tab (nested: /folder/doc/tab/child). A doc with one tab needs no tab step; a doc with several is refused until one is named, and the refusal lists every tab path.","type":"string"},"segment":{"description":"content tree to read (default body)","enum":["body","header","footer","all"],"type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"read_doc","title":"Read a Google Doc"}
